  "id": "COMPOUND:30010 - PROTEIN:6319",
  "verbalization": "Michaolide E is shown to have a target relationship with Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including 6-Methoxysorigenin and (6aR,11aR)-9-hydroxy-3-methoxy-6a,11a-dihydro-6H-[1]benzofuro[3,2-c]chromene-2-carbaldehyde. All these compounds ultimately target UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. This suggests a complex network of interactions where Michaolide E may influence the activity of this enzyme through its interaction with the multidrug resistance-associated protein 7. The evidence supports a mechanism where Michaolide E indirectly modulates UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 by first affecting the multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, which then serves as a bridge to the enzyme. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting the same enzyme highlights the potential for diverse pathways or mechanisms that could contribute to the observed effect. The integration of these pathways underscores the enzyme's role as a downstream target in a multi-compound regulatory network.",
